The install core "yati" from Sphaira (commit 05bd057, 5 November 2026)
  https://github.com/NaGaa95/sphaira
  By ITotalJustice and the Sphaira contributors. GPL-3.0.
  In source/yati and include/yati. Thanks to ITotalJustice and everyone who
  worked on Sphaira: NXDock's installer is built on their work.
  Changed for NXDock on 9 November 2026 (marked "NXDock:" in the code):
  - Sphaira's app, settings, dialogs, translations, log and file system
    helpers are replaced by NXDock's own layer in compat/;
  - the USB, file and stream sources, the MSP installer and the random
    access NCZ reader are left out; NXDock brings its own HTTP source;
  - NCZBLOCK blocks are decompressed on three threads;
  - the NCZSECT2 and NCZSECT3 formats of NXPress are read, the LZ4 blocks of
    an NCZSECT3 made again on the same threads;
  - the install is all or nothing: the free space and the firmware are
    checked first, nothing is registered until every NCA is written and its
    SHA-256 matches its content id, and a failed register is taken back;
  - the user's prod.keys is never read, and tickets are not converted;
  - the control NCA (name and icon) is not read; NXDock gets them from the
    library app.

